From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 06:03:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] isolate: retain a bounded reusable context set

Replace the single saved reusable context with an isolate-local one-window, frequency-protected cache that defaults to five protected residents. Make the protected count a strict self-hosted setting, derive frequency aging and scheduler-wide ownership bounds from it, and keep reusable permits attached to cached and in-flight roots.

Apply this patch after backend memory resilience and consume its shared cgroup-pressure signal. Wake idle workers on transitions, drop fresh and probationary contexts, retain only the two strongest protected entries, suppress new reusable admission, request V8 low-memory collection after removing roots, and let returning protected contexts compete for the pressure-limited capacity.

Separate fresh contexts from reusable residents, use same-client idle workers before creating workers on cache misses, and preserve exact scheduler mirror and capacity invariants. Delay publication through isolate-local finalization, preserve upstream module-wide database reuse for marked queries and mutations, and keep independently gated HTTP reuse intact.

Export bounded normal and cgroup-pressure cache operations, clear reasons, ownership, capacity, and scheduler signals. Document the default 5+1 shape, strict per-isolate and scheduler-pool settings, metric cardinality, and verification expectations.
